  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently, when `pushState()` reaches the limit in Chromium, it just [returns silently](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/history.cc;drc=5f14562c01775211a40ebc3056d0a773c3569008;l=336), whereas in Gecko/Webkit an exception will be raised.  \n\nHere's the step 3 in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#shared-history-push/replace-state-steps \n```\nOptionally, return. (For example, the user agent might disallow calls to these methods that are invoked on a \n\ntimer, or from event listeners that are not triggered in response to a clear user action, or that are invoked in\n\n rapid succession.)\n```\nSo according to the current specification, Chrome's behavior is allowed. \n\nHowever this starts to create webcompat risk, and it looks like Chromium also preferred to have the exception raised. \n\nWhat are people's opinion about this? ",
